Codex CLI

Install:
  Install the global Codex CLI if missing; prepare Node.js/pnpm and configure PATH when installing the CLI.

Upgrade:
  Update the installed Codex CLI through pnpm; prepare Node.js/pnpm as needed.

Status:
  Report the locally available Codex CLI command location and version.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  PNPM_HOME: reuse the persisted Node environment; default ~/.local/share/pnpm
  Open a new terminal after installation to load PATH changes.
  Run codex to sign in; authentication is managed by Codex.
